# A NotClon modchart, as a starting point. This folder is a complete song --
# a chart, a minute of (silent) audio, an actor tree and two shaders -- so it
# runs as-is:
#
#   notclon --dir templates/modchart
#   notclon-editor --mods templates/modchart/example.ncmod
#
# Columns:  tick   *approach   percent   mod   [len=<ticks>]
#
#   tick       beat x Resolution. Resolution is in the chart's [Song] block,
#              almost always 192 -- so beat 16 = tick 3072.
#   *approach  how fast it moves to the target, full swings per second.
#              *-1 snaps instantly, which is the usual choice.
#   percent    100 = full strength. Negative usually mirrors the effect.
#   len=       optional: the value reverts on its own after this many ticks.
#
# See docs/ncmod-format.md for every knob.

# --- what this document loads ------------------------------------------------
# A modchart carries pointers to the chart it was written against and to any
# shaders it drives, so opening it restores the whole thing. Paths are relative
# to THIS file, which is what lets the folder be copied anywhere.
#
# Without these lines the bg.*/fx.* knobs below would drive nothing: the knob
# name comes from a uniform in the shader, so the shader has to be loaded for
# them to mean anything.
#chart templates/modchart
#bgshader shaders/example.frag
#fxshader shaders/playfield.frag

# --- a gentle opening ---------------------------------------------------------
0        *0.5      25        drunk
0        *-1       0         glow

# The background shader's uniforms, as bg.<name>. `bright` defaults to 0 in the
# shader, so a background that is never driven renders black -- that is why it
# is set here from the first tick rather than left to its default.
0        *-1       400       bg.rings
0        *-1       100       bg.warp
0        *2        100       bg.bright

# --- 16 bars in, lean into it -------------------------------------------------
3072     *1        60        drunk
3072     *0.7      40        tornado
3072     *2        30        glow

# --- a stab: one beat of tilt that undoes itself ------------------------------
# This is what len= is for. No second line is needed to put tilt back.
6144     *-1       70        tilt      len=192

# --- the drop -----------------------------------------------------------------
9216     *-1       100       beat
9216     *4        80        bumpy
9216     *-1       40        bumpyspeed
9216     *-1       15        aberration

# --- ...and the playfield shader rides it -------------------------------------
# These are uniforms in shaders/playfield.frag. The percent column is still
# divided by 100, so 900 means 9.0.
9216     *2        900       fx.wobble
9216     *2        600       fx.chroma

# --- a bar of stealth, then back ----------------------------------------------
# 50% stealth turns the notes into white silhouettes rather than hiding them.
12288    *-1       50        stealth   len=768

# --- land it clean ------------------------------------------------------------
15360    *0.6      0         drunk
15360    *0.6      0         tornado
15360    *0.6      0         beat
15360    *0.6      0         bumpy
15360    *1        0         aberration
15360    *1        0         glow
15360    *1        0         fx.wobble
15360    *1        0         fx.chroma

# --- and the background settles with everything else --------------------------
15360    *0.5      0         bg.rings
15360    *0.5      40        bg.warp
